[{"code":"bind_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/BindRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":6,"col":18},"end":{"line":6,"col":19}},"title":"BIND WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `<-`, but I ran into `+`.\n\n`let x <- f a` passes the rest of the block to `f a` as its last argument, so the\nright of `<-` must be the call that receives it — a function, or a call missing\nexactly its final argument. Wrap what you meant in parentheses, or use `=`."},{"code":"bind_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/BindRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":13,"col":14},"end":{"line":13,"col":18}},"title":"BIND WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `<-`, but I ran into `case`.\n\n`let x <- f a` passes the rest of the block to `f a` as its last argument, so the\nright of `<-` must be the call that receives it — a function, or a call missing\nexactly its final argument. Wrap what you meant in parentheses, or use `=`."}]
